    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**1. Missing export in governance module** (src/finetune/index.js)\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named import, but it was only available in the default export\n\n**2. Toxicity metric receiving wrong parameters** (src/eval/metrics.js)\n   - Wrapped `toxicityMetric` in DEFAULT_METRICS as `(outputs) => toxicityMetric(outputs)`\n   - The issue was that `runEvaluations` calls metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` expects `(outputs, bannedTerms)`. References were being interpreted as banned terms, causing false positives\n   - The wrapper ensures only outputs are passed, allowing the function to use default banned terms\n\nAll 28 tests now pass successfully, and the public API remains intact.",
